the same streams.)

===================== 3. READ =====================

- **AomIntraEdgeFilter**: every cell differs from base; the RD effect is
  a small net loss on photo content — median +0.12% (t1) / +0.51% (t3)
  ssim2 BD, PSNR-Y medians +0.01%/+0.07%, means pulled up by a p75 tail
  of ~+1.1%. 18/42 and 11/42 images improve at t1/t3. On gb82-sc it is
  split (t1 median +0.91% ssim2; t3 median −0.22% ssim2 but +0.52%
  PSNR-Y). Encode +1..+4%. Zero failures.
- **AomRestorationUnitSearch**: RD-neutral. Byte-identical in 83% of
  photo and ~98% of screen cells; median BD 0.000 on both axes in every
  arm, means within ±0.07%. Costs +1.6..+9% encode time for no measured
  gain on this grid.
- **AomScreenTools**: NOT inert — but only where designed to act. In the
  briefed grid (p-1/4/6) it is byte-identical in 100% of cells: the fill
  requires the allintra ladder to have killed BOTH palette and IntraBC,
  which first happens at p8. In its active zone under default tune it is
  a large win on real screen content — gb82-sc p8: −23.0% mean ssim2 BD
  (−22.3% median), −28.8% mean PSNR-Y BD (−31.9% median); p10/p12:
  −28.9% / −36.6% mean ssim2/PSNR-Y BD — 9/10 images improve, none
  regress, at +31%..+98% encode time. On photos it fires only where the
  screen detector fires: the 6 winning classes at p8-12 are exactly the
  document/screenshot ones (nps brochures, noaa docs, patent scans,
  plots, mobile + web screenshots); the 15 photo classes stay
  byte-identical, 0 regressions. Under tune IQ it is byte-identical at
  EVERY preset — the IQ bundle's screen_content_mode=3 already derives
  the tools at min(preset,7), leaving no dead-tool state to fill.

===================== 4. HONEST LIMITS =====================

- All-intra 512×512 crops only; presets -1/4/6/8/10/12 (and photo p6);
  no inter claims. Screen n=10; the p8-12 photo arm is 1 image/class
  (n=21); per-image spreads are small-sample.
- Two quality axes only (ssim2 0-100, PSNR-Y). The st wins are on
  detector-positive (screen) content where palette/IntraBC are designed
  to pay; on detector-negative photos it is a proven no-op at every
  measured preset.
- The first sweep run produced 4788 ENC-ERR rows on the 38 LFS-pointer
  inputs (PNG decode InvalidSignature — a harness/data issue, not an
  encoder fault); after materializing the objects those cells encoded
  and decoded clean, and the committed CSV contains only the final
  deduped 10080 rows. Reproducing the photo arm needs
  ~/tmp/aom_kod_images/ (or a materialized imazen-26-png-v3).
- Encode-time ratios measure the identity_run encode process only
  (GNU time U+S around the spawn).
